{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And the word עקרה.</b> It includes both a man's wife and his animal:" "And the fourth, that he too shall live many years. Now we know that every man has a fixed time and a known time that he can live according to the excess of heat and the natural moisture, not foreign fire and alien moisture, for that is contrary to nature. But one who cleaves to the Name — the heat and the moisture are strengthened by the power of the soul, and then the person lives beyond the fixed time. Thus it is written: The fear of YHWH adds days, but the years of the wicked are shortened (Proverbs 10:27); and it is written: In the middle of his days he leaves him (Jeremiah 17:11); and it is written: Whether YHWH strikes him or his day comes (1 Samuel 26 [:10]). Now, one who dies in war or in a plague does not die in his day at the fixed time, according to the nature of the heat and the moisture, for external accidents befell him. And the Name, to one who cleaves to Him, delivers him from them all. And in the Torah: Lest he die in battle (Deuteronomy 20:5). Solomon said: Why die before your time? (Ecclesiastes 7:17). And this is not contrary to the wisdom of the stars, for the matter of the star depends on many things, as I shall explain in the pericope And I shall distinguish, I and Your people (below, 33:16). Therefore it is written: Behold, I add to your days (Isaiah 38:5). And what more shall I add to lengthen?"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {1 "Reading 'והרביעית' as 'the fourth [blessing],' i.e., the fourth blessing listed in the preceding verses (long life, 23:26); the context of Ibn Ezra's surrounding comments enumerating blessings supports this."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:37:51.450848865Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}